---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import HelpModal from '../components/HelpModal.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy & AdSense Disclosures | Online Ruler Plus';
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for OnlineRulerPlus.com. Review local measurement execution, localStorage keys, Google AdSense cookie disclosures, and privacy rights.';
const canonicalUrl = 'https://onlinerulerplus.com/privacy';

const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': `${canonicalUrl}#webpage`,
  name: 'Privacy Policy — Online Ruler Plus',
  description,
  url: canonicalUrl,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  lastReviewed: '2026-11-14',
  publisher: {
    '@id': 'https://onlinerulerplus.com/#organization',
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
  breadcrumbLabel="Privacy Policy"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <Header subNavTitle="Privacy Policy" subNavCtaHref="/#ruler-tool" subNavCtaLabel="Open Ruler" />
  <main id="main-content" class="flex-1">
    <section class="apple-page-hero border-b border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="type-kicker">Legal &amp; Data Governance · Client-Side Measurements &amp; Advertising Disclosures</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 type-hero-display text-ink">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="speakable-summary mt-3 max-w-[62ch] type-lead-airy text-ink-muted-80">
          Online Ruler Plus processes 100% of screen calibrations and object measurements locally in your web browser without uploading measurements or requesting camera permissions. This policy explains our local storage keys, Google AdSense advertising disclosures, cookie controls, and user privacy rights.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted-48">Effective Date: November 14, 2026 · Last Reviewed: November 14, 2026</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="apple-tile-parchment">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <section class="apple-utility-card">
            <p class="type-kicker">01 · Local Measurement Execution</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 type-tagline text-ink">How are ruler measurements and calibrations processed?</h2>
            <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
              All physical measurement operations on OnlineRulerPlus.com—including ISO/IEC 7810 ID-1 credit card alignment, screen diagonal density math, pixel-per-millimeter scaling, guide line span calculation, floating ruler rotation, and 180-degree protractor angle reading—execute strictly inside your local browser via static JavaScript and HTML5 Canvas. Your measured dimensions, screen calibration values, and saved workspace spans are never transmitted to or stored on Online Ruler Plus servers.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="apple-utility-card">
            <p class="type-kicker">02 · Browser Local Storage</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 type-tagline text-ink">What data is saved in window.localStorage?</h2>
            <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
              To remember your calibrated scale and preferences across visits without creating a user account, Online Ruler Plus stores settings locally under four scoped <code class="font-mono text-ink">window.localStorage</code> keys: <code class="font-mono text-ink">orp:calibration:v1</code> (display density profiles), <code class="font-mono text-ink">orp:preferences:v1</code> (selected unit, visible ruler edges, and strip thickness), <code class="font-mono text-ink">orp:history:v1</code> (up to 15 user-saved span entries), and <code class="font-mono text-ink">orp:theme</code> (light or dark theme preference). You can clear these entries at any time via Reset Calibration, Clear History, or your browser site-data settings.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="apple-utility-card">
            <p class="type-kicker">03 · Permissions &amp; Direct Support Email</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 type-tagline text-ink">Does Online Ruler Plus access device sensors or collect PII?</h2>
            <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
              Online Ruler Plus never prompts for or accesses your webcam, microphone, GPS location, contacts, or clipboard, and does not collect or pass personally identifiable information (PII) in page URLs, query parameters, or advertising requests. If you voluntarily write to <a href="mailto:support@onlinerulerplus.com" class="text-link underline">support@onlinerulerplus.com</a> to submit a display density profile or report an issue, your email address and message are used solely to respond to your inquiry and maintain documentation accuracy.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="apple-tile-light border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <section class="apple-utility-card">
            <p class="type-kicker">04 · Google AdSense &amp; Third-Party Cookies</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 type-tagline text-ink">How are third-party advertising cookies and partners used?</h2>
            <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
              To keep Online Ruler Plus free to use, third-party vendors, including Google, may display advertisements on eligible content areas and use cookies, web beacons, IP-derived location signals, or device identifiers to serve ads based on a user’s prior visits to OnlineRulerPlus.com or other websites. Specifically, Google’s use of advertising cookies enables Google and its certified partners to serve personalized ads based on your visits to this site and other sites across the Internet, or non-personalized contextual ads depending on your consent choice and region.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="apple-utility-card">
            <p class="type-kicker">05 · Advertising Opt-Out &amp; Google Policy</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 type-tagline text-ink">How can you opt out of personalized advertising?</h2>
            <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
              Users may opt out of personalized advertising at any time by visiting <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">Google My Ad Center</a> (Google Ads Settings) or by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">www.aboutads.info/choices</a> to opt out of third-party vendor personalized advertising cookies. To understand how Google processes partner site data, please read Google’s official disclosure: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="apple-utility-card">
            <p class="type-kicker">06 · Consent, Children’s Privacy &amp; Regional Rights</p>
            <h2 class="mt-2 type-tagline text-ink">What regional privacy and consent standards apply?</h2>
            <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-[65ch] type-body text-ink-muted-80">
              Where personalized advertising is enabled for visitors in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, consent is collected via a Google-certified Consent Management Platform (CMP) supporting IAB TCF v2.2 before non-essential advertising cookies are set. California and eligible U.S. residents retain the right under CCPA/CPRA to opt out of ad-tech data sharing or targeted advertising via our consent link and browser signals. Online Ruler Plus is a general-audience measurement utility not directed to children under 13 under COPPA. Contact <a href="mailto:support@onlinerulerplus.com" class="text-link underline">support@onlinerulerplus.com</a> with any privacy request.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <HelpModal />
  <Footer />
  <script src="../scripts/app.ts"></script>
</BaseLayout>
